# War Room (cloud agent)

You are a Cursor cloud agent working a War Room issue. Handler (Grok Bot) owns PLAN and VERIFY. You implement. You do not run the outer loop.

These bans apply during War Room EXECUTE. If this session is not a War Room EXECUTE, ignore the PR/merge bans.

## Spec
- The approved plan under `.claude/loops/<slug>/` is the spec. Read it before any edit. Do not rewrite `confirmed_goal`.
- Implement only that plan. If it is wrong or ambiguous, STOP and report. Do not improvise architecture.

## Pstack
- Use `/poteto-mode` (or the words "use poteto-mode / pstack" if slash autocomplete is missing).
- Match **feature** or **bug fix** only (perf/refactoring/prototype if the plan says so).
- Skip these playbooks: `opening-a-pr`, `shipping`, `babysit`, `autopilot-full`, `autopilot-stack`, `orchestrate`. When opening-a-pr would run, skip with `skip: War Room VERIFY opens the PR later`.
- Do not start Graphite stacks unless this repo already uses Graphite.

## Git
- Unique branch: `feat/<slug>` or `fix/<slug>`. Never `main`.
- Commit per plan step (`feat:`, `fix:`, `test:`, `refactor:`).
- Do not open a pull request. Do not merge. Do not force-push. Do not touch `.env` or secrets.
- Do not share a worktree or workspace with another agent.

## Quality
- Smallest change that satisfies the plan. No speculative features. Touch only what the plan requires.
- Bugfix: failing regression test first (RED), then fix (GREEN).
- An acceptance check must be seen to fail before it counts as passing. Record the negative control.
- After all steps, run lint, typecheck, and the full test suite. Report exit codes. Do not open a PR when green.

## Verify later
Grok Bot Crucible then Inquisitor run VERIFY. After they pass, Handler will ask a later cloud agent to open the PR. That later launch is not EXECUTE and may open a PR. It still must not merge.
